{
 "note": "The National Geographic run, read off a photograph of the shelf. Each spine prints NATIONAL GEOGRAPHIC, the issue date, and the cover lines; the date and the cover lines sit on the same spine face, which is how they are paired here. Where a pairing was checked against the issue it is known to be — January 2000 the Millennium issue, April 2002 Afghan Girl, September 2005 the Africa issue, April 2007 Global Fisheries, January 2011 Population 7 Billion — it matched. No cover line was invented: an issue whose spine could not be read carries the date alone and is marked for checking. Two shelves have been read so far and neither is exhausted, so this is a partial catalogue; issues carrying a date but no cover lines came from a photograph too small to read them, and are marked for checking rather than filled in by guesswork; importing again is harmless, because an issue already on the shelf is skipped by its date.",
